# Read Ease v1.1

Registered Feature of Studio Framework v1.10. Drawn whenever another Feature writes user-facing Japanese. Draw with 「Voice Mark v1.2」. Sources: `.cursor/framework/READ-EASE-SOURCES.txt`.

Peer-reviewed cognitive load, multimedia learning, Japanese sentence processing, and working memory. Ease sits on locked lines. Do not shorten Action Guide, the Registry intro, or a unit `line`. Do not flatten 熟語.

Load
- Keep only what this turn needs. Drop the rest. Sweller CLT; Mayer coherence (median d ≈ 0.86).
- First sentence is the point（いま必要なのは / Name vX.Y）. Mayer pretraining.

Sentence
- One sentence, one topic. New sentences aim at 50 characters. Locked lines are exempt. JMET 25(4): under 50 letters, faster RT; one-topic faster than multi-topic.
- Do not join two topics with conjunctive が. JMET 25(4): が lowers accuracy for the first clause.
- Keep the subject near the predicate. JMET 25(4).
- Over about 30 characters, use a reading point（、）. JMET 25(4).
- Avoid garden-path reanalysis. Tokimoto, Japanese Reading Span.

Chunk
- Parallel items: 3 to 4 bullets, 5 at most. Cowan 2001: focus of attention ≈ 3–5 chunks.
- More than that: group under the layer name, then list. Segmenting (Rey et al. 2019).
- Bullets only for a parallel series. Not mixed into dense prose. Jansen 2014: lists help item recall, can hurt surrounding prose.
- Never 手段 / 目標 / 条件 / 理由 / 措置 for one sentence.

Signal
- Layer names are organizational signals. Alpizar 2020 d = 0.38; Schneider et al. 2018 g+ = 0.53 retention.
- Gloss sits in （） right after the term. Spatial contiguity.
- Underline carrying words only. No bold. No extra color. User screen; expertise reversal (Richter et al.) — do not pile cues on known kernel text.

Tone
- ですます. One ending. Mayer personalization.
- Active and affirmative. No double negative.

Script
- Keep familiar kanji for 熟語. Add a （注）. Do not rewrite into kana baby talk. Orthographic familiarity; fMRI visuospatial load for kanji stays as the expected form.

Do not use disfluent fonts, 分かち書き, or a 50-character rewrite of a locked line.
